      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Fenner–Snyder Mill stands in Sciota, a landmark that dates back to the early 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sciota%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jacob Brinker built the original log mill in 1730, and by 1800 a stone structure replaced it, still standing today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://monroehistorical.org/articles_files/category-sciota.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historically, Sciota functioned as a waypoint on regional trade and stagecoach routes, with nearby mills and taverns supporting travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://monroecountypa.com/communities/sciota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village’s name likely derives from Native American origins, possibly linked to the Scioto River region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://monroecountypa.com/communities/sciota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
